#!/bin/sh
# Pre-push QA cleanup rule (issue #62).
# The QA is disposable: test → report → destroy. Before pushing, remove every
# artifact the QA may have created so nothing generated by tests/suites leaks
# into the repository or the environment.
#
# Activation (one-time per clone):
#   git config core.hooksPath .githooks

# Read the ref stream once so both checks can run without losing push metadata.
ref_data=$(cat)

if [ -f scripts/check-issue-references.mjs ]; then
  printf '%s\n' "$ref_data" | node scripts/check-issue-references.mjs
  if [ $? -ne 0 ]; then
    echo "[pre-push] Push rejected: remove issue references from added source lines (comments, strings, or identifiers)." >&2
    exit 1
  fi
fi

if [ -f scripts/qa/cleanup.mjs ]; then
  echo "[pre-push] QA cleanup (disposable artifacts)..."
  node scripts/qa/cleanup.mjs
  if [ $? -ne 0 ]; then
    echo "[pre-push] WARNING: QA cleanup failed — disposable artifacts may remain" >&2
  fi
fi

exit 0
